---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BlogPostHeader from '../../components/BlogPostHeader.astro';

const title = "The Consideration Period: What the New Private Parking Code Says About Airport Drop-offs | AppealAirportPCN";
const description = "From 21 December 2026, the new Private Parking Code gives drivers at least 5 minutes to decide whether to park at an airport drop-off. There is no grace period.";
const canonical = "https://appealairportpcn.co.uk/guides/five-minute-consideration-period/";

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": "The consideration period: what the new Private Parking Code says about airport drop-offs",
  "description": description,
  "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "AppealAirportPCN" },
  "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "AppealAirportPCN.co.uk" },
  "datePublished": "2026-04-15",
  "dateModified": "2026-11-26"
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} schema={schema}>
  <BlogPostHeader title="The consideration period: what the new Private Parking Code says about airport drop-offs" breadcrumbLabel="Consideration period" breadcrumbHref="/guides/five-minute-consideration-period/" updatedDate="NOVEMBER 2026" fixedUpdatedDate={true} />
  <main>
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="blog-post">
        <h2>What a consideration period is</h2>
        <p>A consideration period is the time a driver gets to read the terms and decide whether to accept them. If the driver does not accept, they can leave.</p>
        <p>The new Code lists what the operator must take into account. These include the time to read the signs, the time to pay, and the time to leave. The layout and traffic also count (5.1).</p>
        <p>Entering the land does not, by itself, start the parking contract (2.22). No charge should be issued if a driver considers the terms and chooses not to park (Appeals Charter, 19).</p>

        <h2>What it says about airport drop-offs</h2>
        <p>From 21 December 2026, the new Code sets a minimum consideration period of 5 minutes for short-stay land, including airport drop-off zones (5.2, Annex B). The industry code that applied before that date set a 1-minute minimum.</p>
        <p>There is no grace period at the end of a short-stay period. A grace period is extra time after the permitted period ends. The 5 minutes is time to consider the terms, not free parking.</p>

        <h2>Is it still a ground for appeal?</h2>
        <p>It may help if you were on the land for a very short time and the operator treats entering the site as parking, or ignores that you considered the terms and chose not to park. Check the date of your PCN and the transitional arrangements on GOV.UK.</p>
        <p>If you rely on it, ask the operator for the camera images and accurate time stamps. The new Code requires camera evidence to be checked manually.</p>

        <div class="callout">
          <strong>Key point:</strong> From 21 December 2026, the new Code gives drivers at least 5 minutes to decide whether to park at an airport drop-off. There is no grace period at the end.
        </div>

        <div class="disclaimer">
          <strong>Disclaimer:</strong> This article is for information only and does not constitute legal advice. For complex cases, consult a solicitor or Citizens Advice.
        </div>

        <details class="sources-section">
          <summary>Sources</summary>
        <ol>
          <li>MHCLG, Private Parking Code of Practice (as laid), clauses 2.8, 2.22, 5.1, 5.2 and 19; Annex B. <strong>Primary.</strong> <a href="https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6ad7343784361ce7947cd7c7/Private_Parking_Code_of_Practice.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GOV.UK PDF</a></li>
          <li>Private Parking Sector Single Code of Practice, version 1.1, Annex B (the 1-minute short-stay minimum before 21 December 2026). <strong>Primary.</strong> <a href="https://irp.cdn-website.com/262226a6/files/uploaded/sector+single+Code+of+Practice+Version+1.1+130426-2.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">IPC-hosted PDF</a></li>
        </ol>
        </details>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
